# PHP Rules

- Framework: custom MVC (PHP 7.4) — no Laravel/Symfony conventions
- Namespaces: `Core\`, `Database\`, `Http\`, `Routing\`, `View\`, `Menu\`
- Classes: PascalCase / Methods & variables: camelCase / Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- DB tables use `nb_` prefix (e.g. `nb_siteinfo`, `nb_admin`)
- DB schema changes must go through migration files (`make m`), never alter tables directly

## Patterns

```php
// Routing
$router->get('/', function () {
    return render('pages.index');
})->name('home');

// View rendering
render('pages.index');                        // views/pages/index.php
render('pages.works.view', ['no' => $no]);    // views/pages/works/view.php
```
